# To Whoever Finds This

If you've made it this far, then you've probably found more than I ever managed to.

I spent longer on this than I should have.

At some point, the investigation stopped feeling like an investigation and started feeling like a warning.

Every answer led to another question.

Every name led to another name.

And every time I thought I had finally identified the person behind all of this, I found another record suggesting that I was looking at the wrong face.

I don't think I'm going to find the answer.

Not anymore.

I've gone through the reports. I've gone through the photographs. I've gone through the dates and locations until I stopped being able to tell whether I was finding connections or simply inventing them.

There is still something missing.

One final piece.

I know it's somewhere in the archive. I just don't have the patience—or perhaps the courage—to keep looking for it.

So I'm leaving it to you.

Don't make the same mistake I did.

Don't assume the name tells you who you're looking at.

Don't assume the face does either.

Look at what remains when both are wrong.

If you figure it out, then you'll know more than I ever did.

And if you find the answer...

Well.

Good luck.

You'll need it.

**— The Investigator**
